,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":65.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":null,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":null,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":-0.056272962755601105,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.3041843069117854,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":49.3,"_gate_incr_roic":0.021078480616623384,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":23.7,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":0.1129675177881837,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":85.2,"_gate_rev_durability":0.1087618595962685,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":79.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.10339693450661214,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":76.7,"_gate_margins":-0.002431348783114995,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":47.6,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.01046786643351532,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":22.7,"_gate_share_shrink":0.10355414196472168,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.14363601369030582,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.00066,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.4,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Welltower Inc., an S&P 500 company, is positioned at the center of the silver economy, focusing on rental housing for aging seniors across the United States, United Kingdom, and Canada. Their portfolio of 2,500+ seniors and wellness housing communities are positioned at the intersection of housing and hospitality, creating vibrant communities for mature renters and older adults. They believe our real estate portfolio is unmatched, located in highly attractive micro markets with stunning built environments. Yet, Welltower is an unusual real estate organization as they view themselves as an operating company in a real estate wrapper, driven by highly aligned partnerships and an unconventional culture. Through their disciplined approach to capital allocation powered by their Data Science platform and superior operating results driven by the Welltower Business System - their end-to-end operating platform - they aspire to deliver long-term compounding of per share growth for their existing investors, North Star. Welltower Inc. was incorporated in 1970 in Delaware and is based in Toledo, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Shankh S. Mitra | CEO & Director | Age 44 | Compensation: $7.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 712 people. Revenue per employee of $15.2M ranks in the top quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 16%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $2.6M of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2.2M per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Welltower Inc. is a large-cap real estate business with a $179.3B market cap on $10.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +23% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 2% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $1.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 17 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.08\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 14% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 1098% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":10.981020602003186},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.6pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $2.4M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Welltower Inc. $WELL Stock: Russell Investments Group Ltd. Lowers Position","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/welltower-inc-well-stock-russell-investments-group-ltd-lowers-position.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794568174.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.735,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Welltower Inc. $WELL Stock Purchased by Maryland State Retirement & Pension System","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/welltower-inc-well-stock-purchased-by-maryland-state-retirement-pension-system.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794489765.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.848,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"8,327 Welltower Inc. $WELL Shares Acquired by Walter Public Investments Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/8327-welltower-inc-well-shares-acquired-by-walter-public-investments-inc.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794481028.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Is Welltower (NYSE:WELL) Back in the Spotlight?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/infrastructure-and-real-estate/is-welltower-nysewell-back-in-the-spotlight","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794403920.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Welltower (NYSE:WELL) Price Target Raised to $266.00","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/welltower-nysewell-price-target-raised-to-266-00.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794329690.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"Welltower (WELL) Draws Fresh Interest, Is The Valuation Alre